meta {
  name: Create App Version
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/apps/{{appSlug}}/versions
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-Dev-User-ID: {{devUserId}}
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "git_ref": "v1.2.0"
  }
}

docs {
  Register a new AppVersion at a specific git ref (tag or branch).
  Re-fetches the manifest + evidence at the new SHA, runs Stage-1
  validation, and persists a fresh AuditSubmission so the auditor flow
  can pick it up.

  Validation / behaviour:
    1. Developer role + owning-org check.
    2. Resolve git_ref to a commit SHA via the GitHub App.
    3. Fetch appstore.yaml + run schema validation.
    4. Verify manifest slug matches existing App.slug (slugs are immutable).
    5. Stage-1 evidence validation (fetch + content-type check).
    6. Fetch Chart.yaml + values.schema.json.
    7. Persist AppVersion + AuditSubmission in one transaction.

  Responses:
    201 created        — new version row
    404 not_found      — app slug not found
    403 forbidden      — not in owning org
    409 version_already_exists — same commit SHA already recorded
    422 validation     — manifest or evidence failed
    503 github_not_configured
}
